WEBVTT

1
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.680
<i>I busied myself with a story -</i>

2
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.080
<i>- which would speak to our
mysterious fears -</i>

3
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.320
<i>and awaken thrilling horror.</i>

4
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.600
<i>A story that would make the reader
dread to look around.</i>

5
00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.920
<i>A story that would make the reader
dread to look around.</i>

6
00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.440
The dawn of the 19th century.

7
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.360
A world on the brink of revolution
and scientific advances -

8
00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:15.320
- that would bring profound change.
The lust for knowledge was great.

9
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.240
Among the pioneers,
Captain Robert Walton -

10
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.120
- was obsessed with
reaching the North Pole.

11
00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.080
But his voyage uncovered a story -

12
00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:32.160
- to strike terror into those who
would venture into the unknown...

13
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.360
ARCTIC SEA. 1794

14
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.640
Tell the captain,
we've got to take in the topsaiI.

15
00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:54.160
She's going to rip.

16
00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:03.880
- We have to drop the sails!
- All hands to the mast.

17
00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.040
Take the wheel.

18
00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.640
Captain, we've hit the ice.

19
00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.680
Iceberg ahead!

20
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.960
Hard to starboard!

21
00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.200
Help!

22
00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:59.120
Hold on!

23
00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.640
Put your backs into it, men!

24
00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:27.320
- Let's go!
- Captain, this is useless.

25
00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:32.320
- Should we just lay down and die?
- The men are exhausted.

26
00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:36.440
I have not come this far
to give up now.

27
00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:41.680
They knew the risks. We'Il chop
our way to the Pole if we have to.

28
00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:45.040
Then you
run the risk of mutiny, Captain.

29
00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:50.040
- Did you say mutiny?
- Yes I did. sir.

30
00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:56.160
We proceed north...
as planned.

31
00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:02.720
- At the cost of how many lives?
- As many as it takes!

32
00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:18.440
There's something out there.

33
00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:28.000
What the hell is that?

34
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.160
- Who is your captain?
- I am.

35
00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:01.360
- Who the deviI are you?
- I've no time to talk.

36
00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:04.720
Bring your men and follow me.

37
00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.040
- Now!
- Stay where you are.

38
00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.680
"I" give the orders here.

39
00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.120
Get the dogs!

40
00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.000
Leave them.

41
00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.440
They're already dead.

42
00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:39.800
Get back to the ship.
Everybody, back to the ship!

43
00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:46.800
- Bears don't kill like that!
- Maybe it wants the man.

44
00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.720
Or the captain!

45
00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:54.320
I made my way from St. Petersburg
to ArchangeI on foot.

46
00:05:54.480 --> 00:06:01.120
Then I took a whaling ship north.
When we hit the ice, I used dogs.

47
00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:09.960
What's out there?

48
00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:17.600
I spent six years planning this.
My entire fortune.

49
00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.960
I wilI not be stopped by you
or some phantom.

50
00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:25.640
Do you share my madness?

51
00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:30.080
- No. not madness.
- What then?

52
00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:36.080
There's a passage to the North Pole.
I will find it.

53
00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:42.200
- At the cost of all your lives?
- Lives come and go.

54
00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:47.400
If we succeed.
our names will live on forever.

55
00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:52.040
I will be hailed as
the benefactor of our species.

56
00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:58.160
You're wrong.
I. of all men. know that.

57
00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:00.880
Who are you?

58
00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:05.360
My name...

59
00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.920
...is Victor...

60
00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:12.680
...Frankenstein.

61
00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:22.680
GENEVA. 1773

62
00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:31.280
- Mother!
- My wonderfuI son Victor!

63
00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:38.760
You are the handsomest. kindest
most wonderfuI boy in the world!

64
00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:43.560
Madam!
You will spoil the boy.

65
00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:56.720
- Would you two leave us, please?
- Doctor.

66
00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.760
Come along, Justine.

67
00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:06.000
Victor. this is Elizabeth.
She's coming to live with us.

68
00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:12.200
She's lost her mother and father
to the scarlet fever. Victor.

69
00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:17.400
- She's an orphan now.
- Think of her as your own sister.

70
00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:22.840
You must look after her.
and be kind to her.

71
00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.840
Always.

72
00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:45.880
- How is the imminent arrivaI?
- A little frisky today.

73
00:08:55.000 --> 00:09:00.560
- You used to chase fireflies.
- When I trapped them, they died.

74
00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:04.800
And you cried. You wanted
them to glow by your bedside -

75
00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:07.760
to light you as you read.

76
00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:13.440
You were so hungry for knowledge.
Such a serious little boy.

77
00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:18.280
You've become
such an earnest young man.

78
00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:23.320
All these strange and ancient books.

79
00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:27.880
You'll be a greater doctor
than your father.

80
00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:35.200
But you know, Victor...
Life shouldn't be all study.

81
00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:38.880
There's such fun to be had!

82
00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:42.480
Give me that back. Mother!

83
00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:53.800
Change partners!

84
00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:57.840
Caroline.
you mustn't exert yourself!

85
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:02.200
The new baby
will be a naturaI dancer.

86
00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:10.000
You'll be the envy of
all the young ladies and gentlemen.

87
00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:12.160
Justine!

88
00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:15.640
Justine.
may I have this dance?

89
00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:22.120
Madam!

90
00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:28.040
- You must decide!
- The baby's in the wrong position.

91
00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:35.000
- I can't...
- Cut me to save the baby.

92
00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:48.240
She'll be all right. Your father's
the finest doctor in Geneva.

93
00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:59.480
Father?

94
00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:06.320
Father. how is she?

95
00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:10.520
I did everything I could...

96
00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:15.160
Mother!

97
00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:40.040
Bring her back!
Please, bring her back.

98
00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:45.720
Bring her back!

99
00:11:55.720 --> 00:12:00.280
THREE YEARS LATER

100
00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:13.880
Beloved wife and mother
Caroline Beaufort Frankenstein.

101
00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:18.280
Oh. Mother!

102
00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:24.240
You should never have died.
No one need ever die!

103
00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:27.760
I wilI stop this.

104
00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:33.240
I will stop this.
I promise.

105
00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:37.400
Victor, you're obsessed.
What is that?

106
00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:40.600
Energy.
It never disappears, just changes.

107
00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:44.920
From wax. to
the convulsions of a mechanicaI dog.

108
00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:49.160
The applications are limitless.

109
00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:55.440
- Come outside, it's a lovely day.
- Go away, I'm busy.

110
00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:01.560
What's this?

111
00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:05.640
It's for spraying the electric eels.

112
00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:08.480
Put it down.
It's not for playing with.

113
00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:13.560
It's not for playing with.
Put it down. don't...

114
00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:16.760
Give me that!

115
00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:20.280
Come on!

116
00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:30.440
We should be gratefuI to Victor
for abandoning his experiments.

117
00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:33.480
Well, who says I have?

118
00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:37.960
- What do you mean?
- Look!

119
00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:43.480
- You knew this would happen.
- No, but I hoped it would.

120
00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:45.880
I've never seen one so large.

121
00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:50.520
- Isn't it wonderfuI?
- You shouldn't have done this.

122
00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:56.040
- We must take cover. A tree!
- No, that's the wrong thing.

123
00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:59.880
- What about Willie?
- What are we to do?

124
00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:03.800
Spread out.
Elizabeth. take this.

125
00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:07.600
- Come on, quickly!
- What is that?

126
00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:11.400
- Dig it into the ground.
- Now what?

127
00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:15.760
- Willie!
- Everyone down.

128
00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:19.280
Give me your hand.
It'll be fine.

129
00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:24.280
- I hope you know what you're doing.
- Willie, don't look up!

130
00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:28.560
Wait!
One. two. three...

131
00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:40.560
Now.

132
00:14:54.720 --> 00:15:00.720
- How do you feeI, Elizabeth?
- Alive!

133
00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:34.000
Ladies and gentlemen, friends!
Gather round and listen.

134
00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:39.200
As you probably know,
tomorrow my son Victor leaves me -

135
00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:45.360
- to pursue a career in a profession
that I am not unassociated with.

136
00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:49.000
Modesty!

137
00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:56.080
My one regret is that his mother...

138
00:15:56.240 --> 00:16:00.720
...my late wife, is not here...

139
00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:06.360
...to share the pride...

140
00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:13.040
...which our son
fills me with, tonight.

141
00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:17.520
Yes.

142
00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:27.840
She wanted you to have this,
Victor. On your graduation.

143
00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:31.360
And in it she has written:

144
00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:38.040
"This is the journaI of
Victor Frankenstein."

145
00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:43.360
The rest of the leaves are blank.

146
00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:48.840
- to be filled with the deeds
of a noble life.

147
00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:15.680
We'd better go in,
before they miss us.

148
00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:18.720
Just a little while longer.

149
00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:24.160
I don't know when we'll be
alone together again.

150
00:17:24.920 --> 00:17:27.320
Oh. dear Victor!

151
00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:33.840
- I'Il miss you laughing at me.
- I'll miss you making me laugh.

152
00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:50.320
How do brothers and sisters
say goodbye?

153
00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:56.040
Perhaps they never have to.

154
00:17:56.200 --> 00:18:00.080
I won't, if you won't.

155
00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:16.800
Are you my sister?

156
00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:19.200
Sister...

157
00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:21.880
...friend...

158
00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:24.600
...lover.

159
00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:29.520
- Wife?
- Yes!

160
00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:32.880
- Then come with me. Marry me now!
- No.

161
00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:40.040
- Then I'll stay.
- I want so much to be your wife.

162
00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:44.600
But as long as you're away,
I belong here.

163
00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:50.640
I want to make this house live.
It will be home for our children.

164
00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:56.400
You must go, and do
the great things you need to do.

165
00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:00.920
I want you so much.

166
00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:04.320
I'll be here when you return.

167
00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:08.720
Each holiday. Every visit.

168
00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:16.680
Then, on our wedding night...

169
00:19:25.520 --> 00:19:27.440
Until then.

170
00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:38.240
INGOLSTADT. 1793

171
00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:54.880
- How was yourjourney?
- Very good, thank you.

172
00:19:55.040 --> 00:20:01.160
- We've only got attic space...
- It's exactly what I'm looking for.

173
00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:07.680
But there will be a great deaI
of scientific equipment delivered.

174
00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:12.720
I'm sure you appreciate the need
for a proper laboratory.

175
00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:15.840
Putzi likes you.

176
00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:26.120
This will be perfect.

177
00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:32.480
"The foolish and vain
force their views by the rod."

178
00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:36.640
"But knowledge is power
only through God."

179
00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:42.000
Our motto. Easily forgotten
by you young men in a hurry.

180
00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:50.760
But perhaps the greatest mistake
that all students make.

181
00:20:50.920 --> 00:20:54.480
- during their time here,
is to suppose -

182
00:20:54.640 --> 00:21:00.680
- that they can ever have
an originaI or creative thought.

183
00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:05.120
We have all imagined that
in our time.

184
00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:14.840
But gentlemen, you are not
here to think for yourselves.

185
00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:19.440
You are here to learn
how to think for your patients.

186
00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:29.640
You must learn. therefore. to submit
to the laws of physicaI reality.

187
00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:32.600
But surely, Professor...

188
00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:37.320
- What of philosophicaI approaches?
- PhilosophicaI?

189
00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:42.680
Those of the imagination "and"
the intellect. as in Paracelsus.

190
00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:46.960
Paracelsus?
An arrogant and foolish Swiss.

191
00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:53.560
- Albertus Magnus?
- He was exposed 500 years ago.

192
00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:58.480
- Cornelius Agrippa?
- A sorcerer. What is your name?

193
00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:03.640
Victor Frankenstein.
Of Geneva.

194
00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:06.680
Another Swiss!

195
00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:11.960
Mr. Frankenstein. here at
the University of Ingolstadt -

196
00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:17.640
- we teach the study of medicine.
Chemistry, biology, physics...

197
00:22:17.800 --> 00:22:23.160
- We study hard science.
- Surely they can be combined...

198
00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:29.040
We do not study the ravings
of lunatics and alchemists.

199
00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:37.560
Their fanaticaI speculations
do not heaI bodies or save lives.

200
00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:41.320
Only science can do that.

201
00:22:43.280 --> 00:22:47.920
Now, have we your permission
to continue?

202
00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:57.200
Nice coat. Don't take it too hard.
He doesn't like public humiliation.

203
00:22:57.360 --> 00:23:00.440
- I am not mad!
- Of course you're not.

204
00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:05.720
That's just what a rational person
would say to a complete stranger!

205
00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:09.280
Henry ClervaI.
And I'm completely crazy.

206
00:23:09.440 --> 00:23:13.040
- Victor Frankenstein.
- Of Geneva.

207
00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:17.400
Why don't you look
where I'm going?

208
00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:20.480
That's Schiller.
Ornament of the playing field.

209
00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:24.920
He's new, too. He looks at things
with his mouth open.

210
00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:28.800
What are you here for?

211
00:23:28.960 --> 00:23:33.200
- To research.
- I'm here to become a mere doctor.

212
00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:38.560
A pity it has to do with healing
the sick. I find them revolting.

213
00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:44.040
I'll have a good time, get my degree
if I can stop failing anatomy,

214
00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:50.560
- and then relieve old ladies of
their ailments and their daughters.

215
00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:55.440
- Who was that?
- That's Waldman.

216
00:23:55.600 --> 00:24:00.560
They say in his youth,
he could lecture God on science.

217
00:24:00.720 --> 00:24:05.360
He got into trouble. Something
to do with illegaI experiments.

218
00:24:05.520 --> 00:24:08.320
What kind of experiments,
I wonder?

219
00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:12.240
What was that about
rich old ladies' daughters?

220
00:24:12.400 --> 00:24:16.400
It's a life of sacrifice.
but someone's got to do it.

221
00:24:30.520 --> 00:24:34.040
The centraI nervous system
and the brain -

222
00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:39.800
- are as complicated a set of organs
as you are ever likely to encounter.

223
00:24:39.960 --> 00:24:44.000
Mr. Frankenstein.
the incision is yours.

224
00:24:49.120 --> 00:24:54.560
Excellent. Mr. ClervaI.
you may remove the craniaI lid.

225
00:24:58.560 --> 00:25:01.960
"Henry is still
struggling to pass anatomy."

226
00:25:02.120 --> 00:25:07.280
- I was always terrible at anatomy.
- I'm learning a great deaI.

227
00:25:07.440 --> 00:25:12.120
"Prof. Waldman is remarkable.
God bless you, Victor."

228
00:25:12.280 --> 00:25:16.000
- That's very nice.
- P.S. I've fallen in love.

229
00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:21.040
"She is dark and beautifuI.
and wags her taiI when she sees me."

230
00:25:21.200 --> 00:25:26.080
"Her name is Putzi. and she's the
friendliest sheepdog I've known."

231
00:25:28.040 --> 00:25:32.680
"PS. Elizabeth.
I dream of how your hair shines...

232
00:25:32.840 --> 00:25:39.840
<i>...and of your arms and breasts,
and of our wedding night."</i>

233
00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:44.560
- What does it say?
- "Working hard and making friends".

234
00:25:44.720 --> 00:25:47.440
More coffee, anyone?

235
00:25:48.920 --> 00:25:55.280
Once and for all. Frankenstein!
Life is life. death is death.

236
00:25:55.440 --> 00:25:59.600
- These things are reaI. Absolute.
- Rubbish!

237
00:25:59.760 --> 00:26:03.760
That has been repeatedly challenged.
By "you", sir!

238
00:26:03.920 --> 00:26:09.160
We don't know where death begins.
Hair and nails continue to grow...

239
00:26:09.320 --> 00:26:15.800
Though a man's brain may die, his
heart and lungs continue to pump.

240
00:26:15.960 --> 00:26:22.840
Frankenstein, I warn you what you
suggest is both illegaI and immoraI.

241
00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:25.520
Rubbish!

242
00:26:26.080 --> 00:26:32.000
"Dear diary, why does no one
understand me? PS. I am not mad."

243
00:26:32.920 --> 00:26:35.120
You!

244
00:26:35.280 --> 00:26:40.360
- Explain yourself.
- I came to study the new science.

245
00:26:40.520 --> 00:26:46.440
The combining of modern disciplines
and ancient knowledge to create...

246
00:26:46.600 --> 00:26:49.640
Create what?

247
00:26:49.800 --> 00:26:52.800
We "can" change things.
You know that.

248
00:26:52.960 --> 00:26:57.200
We can make great discoveries
if only we ask the right questions.

249
00:26:57.360 --> 00:26:59.960
You must help me.

250
00:27:02.360 --> 00:27:04.400
Come on.

251
00:27:04.560 --> 00:27:07.480
- Victor...
- Come on.

252
00:27:15.640 --> 00:27:18.080
Henry.

253
00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:33.280
Lock the door.

254
00:27:37.080 --> 00:27:42.320
For thousands of years,
the Chinese have believed -

255
00:27:42.480 --> 00:27:46.440
- that the body is a chemicaI
engine run by energy streams.

256
00:27:46.600 --> 00:27:50.360
- Fascinating! How do they..?
- Don't touch that!

257
00:27:51.640 --> 00:27:56.720
Their doctors treat patients by
inserting needles like these -

258
00:27:56.880 --> 00:28:01.360
- at various key points,
to manipulate the electric streams.

259
00:28:01.520 --> 00:28:07.320
- Electricity is the key!
- Now. look at this.

260
00:28:21.120 --> 00:28:24.600
Go on. touch it.

261
00:28:27.280 --> 00:28:29.320
It feels warm.

262
00:28:30.840 --> 00:28:33.320
How do you do?

263
00:28:34.880 --> 00:28:38.840
- Turn it off!
- I can't, it's not working.

264
00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:44.160
We must simply reduce the polarity.
A monkey's arm is like a human's.

265
00:28:44.320 --> 00:28:49.240
- No arm is this strong!
- Now. this must work.

266
00:28:53.840 --> 00:28:56.440
Let me help you, Professor.

267
00:28:58.280 --> 00:29:02.320
You shall of course tell no one.

268
00:29:02.480 --> 00:29:06.880
No one would believe you, anyway.

269
00:29:09.960 --> 00:29:15.000
Dearest Victor.
Nothing much changes here.

270
00:29:15.160 --> 00:29:20.200
Mrs. Moritz continues to love and
torment Justine, in equaI measure.

271
00:29:20.360 --> 00:29:26.360
Willie grows even more precocious,
and Father is so proud of you.

272
00:29:26.520 --> 00:29:28.520
And I...

273
00:29:28.680 --> 00:29:35.120
I just miss you, very much.
Please write soon. Victor.

274
00:29:35.560 --> 00:29:38.280
Take vaccine. for instance.

275
00:29:38.440 --> 00:29:44.680
30 years ago they were unknown.
But that isn't the whole answer.

276
00:29:44.840 --> 00:29:49.800
- What do you mean?
- We can create life to cheat death.

277
00:29:49.960 --> 00:29:54.400
- No, there's only one God.
- Leave God out of it.

278
00:29:54.560 --> 00:29:59.160
If someone you loved had a sick
heart, would you give them another?

279
00:29:59.320 --> 00:30:06.840
It's not impossible. And if we can
do that, we can replace "every" part.

280
00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:12.040
We can create a being that won't get
old or sick. One better than us.

281
00:30:12.200 --> 00:30:14.920
more intelligent, civilised...

282
00:30:15.080 --> 00:30:18.440
- In our lifetime?
- No!

283
00:30:22.120 --> 00:30:26.840
- How close did you get?
- Too close.

284
00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:31.880
- I beg you, let me see these notes.
- No.

285
00:30:32.040 --> 00:30:37.760
My work now lies exclusively
in the preservation of life.

286
00:30:37.920 --> 00:30:42.040
- I abandoned my other research.
- Why?

287
00:30:43.840 --> 00:30:46.760
Because it resulted in abomination.

288
00:31:05.920 --> 00:31:11.000
- You're not sticking pox in me!
- Pox? They're giving us pox?

289
00:31:11.160 --> 00:31:19.160
- It's harmless anti-pox serum.
- You just said pox!

290
00:31:19.320 --> 00:31:26.320
It's harmless. Without it, this city
would be immediately quarantined.

291
00:31:26.480 --> 00:31:32.240
- You're not sticking that in me.
- Yes I am. It's the law!

292
00:31:32.400 --> 00:31:37.880
- Sit him down.
- You're not sticking that in me!

293
00:31:40.720 --> 00:31:43.120
Professor?

294
00:31:48.040 --> 00:31:51.080
Come on!

295
00:31:51.840 --> 00:31:55.560
It's no use, Victor, he's gone.
Let him go.

296
00:31:55.720 --> 00:31:59.880
- This shouldn't happen!
- Let him go.

297
00:32:00.040 --> 00:32:04.480
It need not happen!

298
00:32:12.160 --> 00:32:15.200
The helI with you!

299
00:32:15.360 --> 00:32:20.680
Whatever you say,
you doctors are killers.

300
00:32:20.840 --> 00:32:25.160
You murder people!
You're eviI!

301
00:32:27.120 --> 00:32:32.480
You're the ones that deserve to die.
God will punish you.

302
00:32:33.640 --> 00:32:36.640
God will punish you.

303
00:32:50.440 --> 00:32:54.960
My God, you were so close!
Of course, the power!

304
00:32:55.120 --> 00:32:59.560
The materials were wrong.
You needed auxiliary sources.

305
00:32:59.720 --> 00:33:03.360
"The experiment... a failure."

306
00:33:03.520 --> 00:33:09.160
"Resulting reanimant
malformed and hideous to behold."

307
00:33:09.320 --> 00:33:14.560
"This factor dependant on the
appropriate raw materials."

308
00:33:17.880 --> 00:33:19.800
Raw materials...

309
00:33:38.280 --> 00:33:43.760
- Come on! What are you afraid of?
- Everything! If the authorities...

310
00:33:43.920 --> 00:33:48.480
We'Il do this in secret.
I've got Waldman's journals.

311
00:33:48.640 --> 00:33:55.400
- You stole Waldman's journals?
- We must complete his work for him.

312
00:33:55.560 --> 00:34:02.000
Were it possible, and you had
the right to make this decision,

313
00:34:02.160 --> 00:34:05.040
- wouldn't there be a
terrible price to pay?

314
00:34:05.200 --> 00:34:12.040
For the chance to defeat death and
disease, to give life to all,

315
00:34:12.200 --> 00:34:17.080
- to allow people who love each
other to be together forever...

316
00:34:17.240 --> 00:34:21.240
I think it's a risk worth taking.

317
00:34:39.360 --> 00:34:42.640
Justine. leave me alone.
I won't talk about it.

318
00:34:43.680 --> 00:34:50.640
- But all the letters you read...
- I wrote them! It's been months...

319
00:34:50.800 --> 00:34:55.320
- Elizabeth...
- Something horrific is happening.

320
00:34:55.480 --> 00:35:00.760
I had to hide it from Father.
Now there are rumours of cholera.

321
00:35:00.920 --> 00:35:06.840
- I can manage here. Go to him!
- He's probably found someone else.

322
00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:10.840
If he was mine.
I'd have gone already.

323
00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:17.440
But he isn't mine.
He's yours, and you must go to him.

324
00:35:31.760 --> 00:35:35.240
Raw materials, that's all they are.

325
00:35:35.400 --> 00:35:38.880
Tissue to be re-used.

326
00:35:45.440 --> 00:35:47.360
The very finest brain.

327
00:35:59.360 --> 00:36:03.600
- But they all died of cholera, sir.
- No matter.

328
00:36:10.680 --> 00:36:15.560
The assembled organs must have
nutrients, heat, and crucially...

329
00:36:15.720 --> 00:36:20.240
...more direct power.

330
00:36:23.640 --> 00:36:26.440
More direct power...

331
00:36:47.160 --> 00:36:51.000
Amniotic fluid is the
chief biogenic element.

332
00:36:51.160 --> 00:36:54.760
Acupuncture needles are
inserted at energy points.

333
00:36:54.920 --> 00:36:58.640
When the current stops,
the dead toad has animation -

334
00:36:58.800 --> 00:37:02.680
- independently
of externaI power sources.

335
00:37:11.080 --> 00:37:15.320
Yes. That's it.

336
00:37:15.480 --> 00:37:19.640
That's the combination!

337
00:38:21.720 --> 00:38:24.280
Victor!

338
00:38:24.440 --> 00:38:27.640
Open the door!

339
00:38:27.800 --> 00:38:32.280
- What do you want?
- There's cholera. An epidemic!

340
00:38:32.440 --> 00:38:37.480
The city is under martiaI law.
Are you listening to me?

341
00:38:37.640 --> 00:38:42.000
The militia's quarantining the city.
We're getting out.

342
00:38:42.600 --> 00:38:45.680
What if Krempe
tells the authorities?

343
00:38:45.840 --> 00:38:48.360
Goodbye, Henry.

344
00:38:48.520 --> 00:38:52.800
Victor. it's me. Elizabeth.

345
00:38:55.040 --> 00:38:59.720
Can you hear me?
I have to see you.

346
00:39:01.440 --> 00:39:05.280
- Go away.
- Please. Victor!

347
00:39:07.240 --> 00:39:11.520
I won't leave here
until you see me.

348
00:39:17.280 --> 00:39:20.480
Come in the side door.

349
00:39:21.000 --> 00:39:23.920
Alone!

350
00:39:35.240 --> 00:39:38.800
What's happened to you?

351
00:39:38.960 --> 00:39:42.200
How can you live here like this?

352
00:39:42.360 --> 00:39:46.280
- And that stench...
- Don't go in there!

353
00:39:50.280 --> 00:39:54.080
- We have to leave. It isn't safe.
- No, I must stay.

354
00:39:54.240 --> 00:39:57.840
- Even if it means you'll die?
- Yes.

355
00:40:09.280 --> 00:40:15.360
- Well, let me help you.
- No, that's impossible.

356
00:40:18.440 --> 00:40:22.560
We made a promise.

357
00:40:26.720 --> 00:40:30.120
Victor, I beg you.

358
00:40:32.560 --> 00:40:36.760
I know this is difficult for you
to understand.

359
00:40:36.920 --> 00:40:42.200
- but I cannot
abandon this work now.

360
00:40:42.360 --> 00:40:48.000
It's too important. Not just for me,
but, believe me, for everyone.

361
00:40:50.960 --> 00:40:55.640
And it must come first.

362
00:40:59.400 --> 00:41:01.400
Before us?

363
00:41:05.840 --> 00:41:08.520
Elizabeth...

364
00:41:08.680 --> 00:41:12.560
I love you so much, but...

365
00:41:23.920 --> 00:41:26.000
Goodbye.

366
00:41:48.320 --> 00:41:50.840
Elizabeth!

367
00:41:54.320 --> 00:41:58.120
Oh God! Elizabeth.

368
00:43:53.320 --> 00:43:55.680
Live! Live!

369
00:44:00.080 --> 00:44:02.720
Yes!

370
00:44:18.080 --> 00:44:22.200
No...

371
00:44:46.720 --> 00:44:49.760
It's alive...

372
00:44:50.720 --> 00:44:54.200
It's alive!

373
00:46:57.680 --> 00:47:01.000
What have I done?

374
00:47:04.960 --> 00:47:08.240
What have I done?

375
00:47:18.880 --> 00:47:23.560
Massive birth defects...

376
00:47:23.720 --> 00:47:28.520
...greatly enhanced
physicaI strength...

377
00:47:28.680 --> 00:47:30.640
...but...

378
00:47:30.800 --> 00:47:34.320
...resulting reanimant...

379
00:47:34.480 --> 00:47:38.480
...is malfunctionaI...

380
00:47:38.640 --> 00:47:41.520
...and pitifuI...

381
00:47:41.920 --> 00:47:45.720
...and dead.

382
00:47:49.080 --> 00:47:54.200
Tomorrow this journaI and
its secrets must be destroyed...

383
00:47:55.120 --> 00:47:57.040
...forever.

384
00:48:09.440 --> 00:48:12.280
Oh. God!

385
00:48:58.480 --> 00:49:00.120
No!

386
00:49:00.280 --> 00:49:04.560
You fooI.
Victor Frankenstein of Geneva!

387
00:49:04.720 --> 00:49:08.080
How could you know
what you'd unleashed?

388
00:49:08.240 --> 00:49:13.560
How is it pieced together?
Bits of thieves and murderers...

389
00:49:13.720 --> 00:49:17.160
EviI stitched to eviI.
stitched to eviI...

390
00:49:17.320 --> 00:49:22.480
Do you really think this thing
will thank you for its birth?

391
00:49:22.640 --> 00:49:26.080
EviI will have its revenge.

392
00:49:26.520 --> 00:49:30.280
God help your loved ones!

393
00:50:42.440 --> 00:50:46.040
What do you think you're doing?

394
00:50:46.200 --> 00:50:51.200
He's got cholera!
He's been spreading the plague!

395
00:51:27.760 --> 00:51:30.720
Get him!

396
00:51:36.360 --> 00:51:40.400
- Keep away from him.
- No. kill him now!

397
00:51:55.960 --> 00:51:59.240
He went this way.

398
00:52:44.320 --> 00:52:48.760
There now. Easy.
Just a bit.

399
00:52:50.040 --> 00:52:55.480
- That's it. There now, rest easy.
- Henry, you're here.

400
00:52:55.640 --> 00:53:00.360
Of course I'm here.
But it was touch and go with you.

401
00:53:00.520 --> 00:53:04.880
I feared cholera.
but it turned out to be pneumonia.

402
00:53:05.040 --> 00:53:09.680
I'm becoming a doctor.
Even Krempe seems pleased with me.

403
00:53:09.840 --> 00:53:12.920
At this rate.
I might even pass anatomy.

404
00:53:13.080 --> 00:53:19.120
- The epidemic?
- There's nothing we can do.

405
00:53:19.280 --> 00:53:25.320
The vulnerable, anyone without
shelter. the new-born. will die.

406
00:53:25.480 --> 00:53:28.640
- Are you sure?
- I'm certain of it.

407
00:53:29.840 --> 00:53:35.080
- Thank God.
- What do you mean?

408
00:53:41.760 --> 00:53:43.720
Nothing.

409
00:53:47.040 --> 00:53:51.360
Well then.
that's my shift finished.

410
00:53:54.960 --> 00:53:58.400
I'll see you later.

411
00:54:46.200 --> 00:54:49.680
Elizabeth...

412
00:55:02.560 --> 00:55:05.680
Elizabeth!

413
00:55:14.600 --> 00:55:19.320
- Please, please, forgive me!
- Of course I do.

414
00:55:22.280 --> 00:55:28.560
I don't know what you're working on,
but it nearly killed you.

415
00:55:29.720 --> 00:55:33.760
It's over. it's finished.
It should never have started.

416
00:55:33.920 --> 00:55:37.440
It's dead!

417
00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:34.640
Felix!
Don't forget the onion scraps.

418
00:56:34.800 --> 00:56:38.240
All right, I've got them.

419
00:56:38.400 --> 00:56:41.480
Go on, get!

420
00:56:44.040 --> 00:56:47.360
Go on, go on!

421
00:57:00.800 --> 00:57:05.280
- How are the pigs?
- Happy, they've been fed.

422
00:57:05.440 --> 00:57:10.400
- How are your hands?
- They're bleeding again.

423
00:57:16.840 --> 00:57:20.280
That's better.

424
00:57:23.440 --> 00:57:25.840
There.

425
00:57:26.000 --> 00:57:31.360
- The soup's ready.
- Come on, Grandpa. Sit down.

426
00:58:28.520 --> 00:58:32.840
We'll never get through the winter
with this yield.

427
00:58:33.000 --> 00:58:36.680
- The ground's frozen hard.
- We'll sell another pig.

428
00:58:36.840 --> 00:58:41.360
We can't.
Not until they lift the quarantine.

429
00:58:41.520 --> 00:58:45.320
Even then. it's one less for us.
And there's last month's rent...

430
00:58:45.480 --> 00:58:49.640
Come on!
We'll do this together.

431
00:58:52.480 --> 00:58:57.800
You're right.
We've got to, before the snow comes.

432
00:59:04.480 --> 00:59:07.040
Come on. then!

433
00:59:23.120 --> 00:59:29.600
The ground's frozen solid. We'd need
20 men to do this. It's useless!

434
00:59:29.760 --> 00:59:33.440
- It's getting late.
- We don't have enough to eat.

435
00:59:33.600 --> 00:59:36.680
We'll manage.
Let's go.

436
00:59:59.240 --> 01:00:02.800
Look!

437
01:00:12.520 --> 01:00:18.880
- They're from the Forest Spirit.
- Father, nothing is free of cost.

438
01:00:19.040 --> 01:00:24.520
- I would like to know who and why.
- Was it the Good Spirit, Grandpa?

439
01:00:24.680 --> 01:00:29.080
- I believe it was.
- Don't fill them with nonsense.

440
01:00:48.040 --> 01:00:50.920
Who's there?

441
01:00:51.080 --> 01:00:54.000
Felix?
Children?

442
01:01:03.120 --> 01:01:07.720
FRIEND

443
01:01:09.280 --> 01:01:15.280
- What's this one?
- Fr... i... end.

444
01:01:16.440 --> 01:01:21.480
- Friend?
- Friend! Well done!

445
01:01:22.800 --> 01:01:28.000
You've got lots of friends,
haven't you? Grandpa...

446
01:01:29.400 --> 01:01:34.320
Frieeend...

447
01:02:02.280 --> 01:02:05.200
Friend.

448
01:02:06.080 --> 01:02:09.280
Family.

449
01:02:10.240 --> 01:02:13.680
F... Father.

450
01:02:15.280 --> 01:02:19.760
Travel with them. The equipment
must not be left unattended.

451
01:02:19.920 --> 01:02:23.640
- My father wilI take delivery.
- Yes. sir.

452
01:02:23.800 --> 01:02:28.560
- Going somewhere?
- Look at the locket Victor gave me.

453
01:02:28.720 --> 01:02:35.280
- Lovely! Is it really you?
- It will serve instead of a ring.

454
01:02:35.440 --> 01:02:38.440
Congratulations
on the entirely expected!

455
01:02:38.600 --> 01:02:42.080
- When?
- As soon as we get home.

456
01:02:43.120 --> 01:02:47.320
- He's to have Father's practice.
- And expand it.

457
01:02:47.480 --> 01:02:51.760
- I'm going on ahead.
- A practice needs a partner...

458
01:02:51.920 --> 01:02:57.360
There's not much money, but
there's food and board and company.

459
01:02:57.520 --> 01:03:02.640
It's the ideaI position for someone
who's finally passed anatomy.

460
01:03:02.800 --> 01:03:07.440
So we were wondering if...
you could recommend someone?

461
01:03:09.240 --> 01:03:14.720
- I don't know what to say.
- Please, say yes.

462
01:03:15.360 --> 01:03:17.600
Yes!

463
01:03:17.760 --> 01:03:21.400
Yes!

464
01:03:21.560 --> 01:03:25.520
And you can write that down
in yourjournaI!

465
01:03:39.080 --> 01:03:41.920
"This is..."

466
01:03:42.080 --> 01:03:46.080
"... the journaI..."

467
01:03:46.240 --> 01:03:48.920
"... of..."

468
01:03:49.080 --> 01:03:51.880
"... Victor..."

469
01:03:53.000 --> 01:03:55.880
"... Frankenstein..."

470
01:03:56.040 --> 01:03:58.160
"... of..."

471
01:03:58.320 --> 01:04:01.680
"... Geneva."

472
01:04:04.720 --> 01:04:08.520
Come on, quickly.

473
01:04:11.000 --> 01:04:16.000
- Merry Christmas!
- Come on. time for bed.

474
01:04:26.320 --> 01:04:32.440
"For the Good Spirit of the Forest."

475
01:04:46.080 --> 01:04:52.560
- Are you the Good Spirit?
- Not exactly. Where's your father?

476
01:04:52.720 --> 01:04:56.040
I said, where's your father?

477
01:04:56.200 --> 01:05:00.160
- Maggie?
- No.

478
01:05:00.320 --> 01:05:05.360
- What have you done to Maggie?
- Is he in there, hiding behind you?

479
01:05:05.520 --> 01:05:07.840
Get away!

480
01:05:09.320 --> 01:05:12.200
Don't blame me.

481
01:05:12.360 --> 01:05:17.160
Blame your son,
for not paying his rent on time.

482
01:05:27.600 --> 01:05:29.680
My God!

483
01:05:30.560 --> 01:05:34.360
Thank you, my friend.
Thank you so much.

484
01:05:36.440 --> 01:05:40.280
Won't you come and sit by the fire?

485
01:05:40.440 --> 01:05:43.320
Please. don't be afraid.

486
01:05:44.720 --> 01:05:47.920
Come.
Come in.

487
01:05:56.280 --> 01:05:59.840
Have a rest. sit down.

488
01:06:01.400 --> 01:06:04.800
That's better.

489
01:06:04.960 --> 01:06:08.080
I'm glad you finally came in.

490
01:06:08.240 --> 01:06:13.360
A man shouldn't have to hide
in the shadows.

491
01:06:18.720 --> 01:06:23.400
Better that way, for me.

492
01:06:23.560 --> 01:06:25.560
Why?

493
01:06:27.120 --> 01:06:30.920
People are afraid.

494
01:06:31.080 --> 01:06:33.920
Except you.

495
01:06:35.200 --> 01:06:38.960
It can't be as bad as that.

496
01:06:42.000 --> 01:06:46.040
Worse.

497
01:06:46.200 --> 01:06:52.360
I can "see" you with my hands,
if you'll trust me.

498
01:07:11.280 --> 01:07:14.200
- Papa, he hurt Grandpa!
- Who did?

499
01:07:14.360 --> 01:07:18.040
What was that noise?
What happened, Maggie?

500
01:07:18.960 --> 01:07:22.160
Poor man.

501
01:07:26.360 --> 01:07:30.160
Have you no friends?

502
01:07:31.640 --> 01:07:36.760
There are some people...

503
01:07:40.880 --> 01:07:44.600
But they don't know me.

504
01:07:44.760 --> 01:07:48.360
Why do you not go to them?

505
01:07:52.080 --> 01:07:57.720
Because I am so very...

506
01:08:03.120 --> 01:08:06.440
...ugly.

507
01:08:07.000 --> 01:08:12.680
And they are so very...

508
01:08:17.120 --> 01:08:19.560
...beautifuI.

509
01:08:19.720 --> 01:08:22.120
Father!

510
01:08:22.280 --> 01:08:27.840
- Get out of here. monster.
- Leave him alone!

511
01:08:31.400 --> 01:08:33.520
We have to leave here.

512
01:09:20.480 --> 01:09:23.760
No...

513
01:09:33.480 --> 01:09:37.960
Massive birth defects...
greatly enhanced strength...

514
01:09:38.120 --> 01:09:40.760
...dead.
These experiments are at an end.

515
01:10:05.880 --> 01:10:10.680
I will have revenge!

516
01:10:11.760 --> 01:10:15.360
Frankenstein!

517
01:10:47.320 --> 01:10:50.360
Geneva!

518
01:11:03.320 --> 01:11:09.880
- Quickly!
- She's here! We got your letter.

519
01:11:10.040 --> 01:11:14.760
- Congratulations, Elizabeth.
- Thank you, Justine.

520
01:11:14.920 --> 01:11:17.920
Is that the locket?

521
01:11:18.080 --> 01:11:22.000
- Look how handsome Victor is!
- Can I take this to show Peter?

522
01:11:22.160 --> 01:11:25.200
- It's not a toy.
- Let him go.

523
01:11:33.600 --> 01:11:39.560
Justine, pay attention! Anyone
would think "you're" getting married.

524
01:11:39.720 --> 01:11:42.760
- What's wrong?
- Nothing.

525
01:11:42.920 --> 01:11:46.560
Leave it.
You've ruined it. now.

526
01:12:12.720 --> 01:12:16.280
No!

527
01:12:27.280 --> 01:12:30.240
Frankenstein.

528
01:12:31.800 --> 01:12:34.960
- You, quickly!
- Have you seen Willie?

529
01:12:35.120 --> 01:12:41.320
- They say he never arrived.
- Far too late for him to be out.

530
01:12:46.480 --> 01:12:48.760
William!

531
01:12:51.720 --> 01:12:54.520
Willie!

532
01:12:54.680 --> 01:12:57.320
Willie!

533
01:13:08.280 --> 01:13:12.120
This isn't a game!

534
01:13:18.400 --> 01:13:22.120
It's so late.

535
01:13:22.280 --> 01:13:27.640
We're all so tired.
I'm so tired.

536
01:13:29.120 --> 01:13:33.760
Father!
I'm so pleased to see you.

537
01:13:38.640 --> 01:13:40.560
What's wrong?

538
01:14:00.240 --> 01:14:03.480
<i>William!</i>

539
01:14:10.880 --> 01:14:14.640
We checked the east ridge.
There's nothing there.

540
01:14:18.720 --> 01:14:26.600
- Elizabeth?
- I've found him.

541
01:14:29.360 --> 01:14:32.720
Elizabeth!

542
01:14:32.880 --> 01:14:36.040
No!

543
01:15:06.560 --> 01:15:10.440
We did everything we could, sir.

544
01:15:10.600 --> 01:15:14.840
You just rest easy now.
We did everything we could.

545
01:15:16.040 --> 01:15:21.280
Sir, I'm terrified for my girI.
She's still out looking for William.

546
01:15:21.440 --> 01:15:26.000
We parted badly. I was crueI to her.
I didn't mean it.

547
01:15:26.160 --> 01:15:32.520
I think she finds it hard, with your
wedding. She loves you dearly.

548
01:15:32.680 --> 01:15:37.880
I couldn't bear it if anything
happened to her. Help me!

549
01:15:39.320 --> 01:15:42.920
We'll organise another search.

550
01:15:43.080 --> 01:15:46.720
We will find her. Mrs. Moritz.

551
01:15:48.680 --> 01:15:53.120
- How is Father?
- His heart is breaking.

552
01:16:01.240 --> 01:16:08.000
Mr. Frankenstein, we've apprehended
the murderer, hiding in a barn.

553
01:16:09.040 --> 01:16:13.680
We found this on her.
It's yours, I believe?

554
01:16:16.080 --> 01:16:21.520
Sir, you must come immediately.
The townspeople have gone mad.

555
01:16:23.960 --> 01:16:28.480
- What are they doing?
- They've broken into the jaiI!

556
01:16:28.640 --> 01:16:31.280
This is a Iynching mob!

557
01:16:31.440 --> 01:16:35.360
Stop!
This is unlawfuI.

558
01:16:43.560 --> 01:16:47.920
Victor, help me.
I was trying to find him.

559
01:16:48.640 --> 01:16:53.960
I went to the lake.
I wanted to bring him to you.

560
01:16:54.120 --> 01:17:00.360
He must be there for the wedding!
I'm sorry! He's so tiny.

561
01:17:35.000 --> 01:17:39.520
We've closed the gates on the mob.
What about Justine?

562
01:17:39.680 --> 01:17:45.280
- We've cut her down.
- Thank you, Claude. Get to bed.

563
01:17:51.080 --> 01:17:53.200
The Sea of Ice.

564
01:17:54.400 --> 01:17:56.600
I will meet you there...

565
01:17:56.760 --> 01:18:00.720
...on the Sea of Ice.

566
01:18:18.320 --> 01:18:20.240
Justine, forgive me.

567
01:18:21.280 --> 01:18:25.720
Who is this man?
How do you know he's responsible?

568
01:18:25.880 --> 01:18:29.520
- I'll tell you after I destroy him.
- Leave it to the police.

569
01:18:29.680 --> 01:18:33.520
- They wouldn't understand.
- Neither do I.

570
01:18:34.800 --> 01:18:38.400
Then just accept it.

571
01:20:20.720 --> 01:20:23.800
Get up.

572
01:20:23.960 --> 01:20:28.880
- You "do" speak.
- Yes, I speak.

573
01:20:29.040 --> 01:20:32.320
And read.

574
01:20:32.480 --> 01:20:35.600
And think.

575
01:20:35.760 --> 01:20:40.400
- And know the ways of man.
- How did you find me?

576
01:20:44.800 --> 01:20:48.440
YourjournaI.

577
01:20:50.360 --> 01:20:53.560
Then you mean to kill me.

578
01:20:53.720 --> 01:20:56.800
No.

579
01:20:57.480 --> 01:21:00.680
You murdered my brother,
didn't you?

580
01:21:02.880 --> 01:21:07.240
I took him by the throat
with one hand.

581
01:21:07.400 --> 01:21:11.200
lifted him off the ground,

582
01:21:11.360 --> 01:21:15.400
and slowly crushed his neck.

583
01:21:17.680 --> 01:21:24.000
And as I killed him.
I saw your face.

584
01:21:26.040 --> 01:21:32.000
You gave me these emotions. But
you didn't tell me how to use them.

585
01:21:33.160 --> 01:21:36.720
Now two people are dead...

586
01:21:36.880 --> 01:21:40.360
...because of us.

587
01:21:41.280 --> 01:21:44.440
Why?

588
01:21:44.600 --> 01:21:49.840
There's something at work in my souI
which I do not understand.

589
01:21:51.720 --> 01:21:55.520
What of my souI?
Do I have one?

590
01:21:55.680 --> 01:21:59.880
Or was that a part you left out?

591
01:22:00.920 --> 01:22:05.760
Who were these people
of which I am comprised?

592
01:22:06.800 --> 01:22:10.600
Good people? Bad people?

593
01:22:10.760 --> 01:22:15.920
- Materials, nothing more.
- You're wrong.

594
01:22:16.880 --> 01:22:21.080
Do you know
I knew how to play this?

595
01:22:21.240 --> 01:22:25.320
In which part of me
did this knowledge reside?

596
01:22:25.480 --> 01:22:27.840
In these hands?

597
01:22:28.000 --> 01:22:31.480
In this mind?
In this heart?

598
01:22:31.640 --> 01:22:36.400
And reading and speaking...

599
01:22:37.800 --> 01:22:43.560
Not things learned,
so much as things remembered.

600
01:22:44.800 --> 01:22:48.400
Trace memories in the brain.
perhaps.

601
01:22:49.640 --> 01:22:55.600
Did you ever consider
the consequences of your actions?

602
01:22:56.600 --> 01:23:02.680
You gave me life,
and then you left me to die.

603
01:23:08.320 --> 01:23:12.560
- Who am I?
- You...

604
01:23:17.160 --> 01:23:20.960
I don't know.

605
01:23:22.400 --> 01:23:26.840
And you think "I'm" eviI.

606
01:23:27.840 --> 01:23:30.560
What can I do?

607
01:23:30.720 --> 01:23:34.960
There is something I want.
A friend.

608
01:23:35.120 --> 01:23:38.840
- A friend?
- Companion.

609
01:23:39.000 --> 01:23:44.760
A female.
Someone like me.

610
01:23:45.760 --> 01:23:50.640
- So she won't hate me.
- Like you?

611
01:23:52.280 --> 01:23:55.360
You don't know what you're asking.

612
01:23:55.520 --> 01:24:03.440
I do know that for
the sympathy of one living being -

613
01:24:03.600 --> 01:24:08.360
I would make peace with all.

614
01:24:10.240 --> 01:24:17.240
I have love in me the likes of which
you can scarcely imagine.

615
01:24:18.520 --> 01:24:24.880
And rage, the likes of which
you would not believe.

616
01:24:26.840 --> 01:24:32.160
If I cannot satisfy the one...

617
01:24:32.600 --> 01:24:37.640
...I will indulge the other.

618
01:24:40.160 --> 01:24:46.480
And if I consent, how will you live?

619
01:24:49.440 --> 01:24:56.760
We would traveI north.
to the furthest reaches of the Pole.

620
01:24:56.960 --> 01:25:01.080
Where no man has ever set foot.

621
01:25:01.240 --> 01:25:08.120
There we would
live out our lives together.

622
01:25:09.160 --> 01:25:13.880
No human eye
would ever see us again.

623
01:25:15.200 --> 01:25:19.520
This. I vow.

624
01:25:19.680 --> 01:25:24.400
You must help me.
Please.

625
01:25:28.000 --> 01:25:32.880
If it is possible
to right this wrong...

626
01:25:34.160 --> 01:25:37.320
...then I will do it.

627
01:25:37.480 --> 01:25:40.200
Victor!

628
01:25:40.360 --> 01:25:43.120
Are you all right?

629
01:25:44.160 --> 01:25:48.320
- Yes. I'm safe.
- What happened?

630
01:25:48.520 --> 01:25:51.360
Tell us.

631
01:25:55.680 --> 01:25:58.840
You have to tell us what happened!

632
01:25:59.000 --> 01:26:03.960
One month. that's all. Then we can
be married and forget all this.

633
01:26:04.120 --> 01:26:07.320
- I promise.
- Promise!

634
01:26:07.480 --> 01:26:12.480
You "promised" to tell me who he was.
You "promised" to stop this work.

635
01:26:12.640 --> 01:26:16.760
- I have to leave this house.
- Where wilI you go?

636
01:26:16.920 --> 01:26:20.920
- Somewhere I can recover.
- I haven't got time to argue.

637
01:26:21.080 --> 01:26:24.480
Doesn't it fit in with your plans?

638
01:26:24.640 --> 01:26:28.800
Don't you ever think
of anyone but yourself?

639
01:26:39.080 --> 01:26:42.520
God forgive me!

640
01:28:02.040 --> 01:28:04.920
Why her?

641
01:28:05.080 --> 01:28:10.800
Materials. remember?
Nothing more. Your words.

642
01:28:12.880 --> 01:28:17.280
- You will honour your promise!
- I will not.

643
01:28:17.440 --> 01:28:21.280
- Go on. kill me now!
- That is too mild.

644
01:28:21.440 --> 01:28:25.440
If you deny me my wedding night,
I will be with you on yours!

645
01:28:27.600 --> 01:28:30.920
Elizabeth!

646
01:28:32.240 --> 01:28:35.240
Wait.

647
01:28:35.840 --> 01:28:39.000
I have to speak to you.
Please!

648
01:28:48.280 --> 01:28:51.680
What do you want to say?

649
01:28:51.840 --> 01:28:54.920
Don't go.

650
01:28:56.000 --> 01:29:00.560
Please, don't go.

651
01:29:06.200 --> 01:29:08.520
I'm frightened.

652
01:29:11.560 --> 01:29:15.040
Of what?

653
01:29:17.600 --> 01:29:23.280
I have done something
so terrible...

654
01:29:24.560 --> 01:29:28.000
So eviI...

655
01:29:29.680 --> 01:29:35.240
And I'm frightened
that if I tell you the truth...

656
01:29:36.920 --> 01:29:40.560
...that I will lose you.

657
01:29:41.240 --> 01:29:44.120
You'll lose me if you don't.

658
01:29:47.600 --> 01:29:50.320
I...

659
01:29:50.480 --> 01:29:53.920
...don't know...

660
01:29:56.080 --> 01:29:59.160
...what...

661
01:29:59.320 --> 01:30:02.360
...to do.

662
01:30:35.880 --> 01:30:39.480
Will you marry me, Victor?

663
01:30:41.920 --> 01:30:45.640
Marry me today.

664
01:30:45.800 --> 01:30:50.520
Tomorrow, tell me everything.

665
01:30:51.760 --> 01:30:55.080
But you must tell me the truth.

666
01:30:56.920 --> 01:31:01.280
And together, we can face anything.

667
01:31:02.120 --> 01:31:07.960
Whatever you've done,
whatever has happened...

668
01:31:09.440 --> 01:31:12.360
...I love you.

669
01:31:21.360 --> 01:31:27.440
To share the truth. the whole truth.
for good or ill,

670
01:31:27.600 --> 01:31:33.800
- to stand by each other
in sickness and in health.

671
01:31:34.000 --> 01:31:39.560
- and in joy,
from this day forward -

672
01:31:39.720 --> 01:31:44.320
until death do you part.

673
01:31:59.520 --> 01:32:03.200
- Who is he? How shall we know him?
- You'll know him.

674
01:32:03.360 --> 01:32:09.640
He killed William. and Justine
died for it. Shoot him on sight!

675
01:32:11.280 --> 01:32:15.960
You two look after each other.
I'll look after your father.

676
01:32:58.280 --> 01:33:02.880
The last ferry's gone.
There's nothing now 'till morning.

677
01:33:03.040 --> 01:33:06.680
- I'll find lodgings for you.
- Thank you, Claude.

678
01:33:10.760 --> 01:33:14.040
- Keep your pistols dry!
- They're dry enough.

679
01:33:14.200 --> 01:33:19.520
- If they faiI, we'll gut him.
- Go to your post.

680
01:33:21.880 --> 01:33:26.040
Don't worry, sir.
You're well guarded.

681
01:33:26.200 --> 01:33:31.840
Go up to your wife. It's not often
a man has his wedding night.

682
01:33:55.880 --> 01:33:59.320
You're soaking.

683
01:34:06.800 --> 01:34:10.560
Brother and sister...
no more.

684
01:34:10.720 --> 01:34:13.640
Now husband and wife.

685
01:35:35.520 --> 01:35:38.280
Victor?

686
01:35:39.440 --> 01:35:42.360
Lock the door.

687
01:35:45.000 --> 01:35:48.760
- I saw him. He ran to the lake.
- You two stay here.

688
01:35:59.880 --> 01:36:04.480
- We lost him.
- Elizabeth!

689
01:36:05.320 --> 01:36:08.640
Don't bother to scream.

690
01:36:25.360 --> 01:36:31.080
Please...
Please don't hurt me.

691
01:36:31.680 --> 01:36:36.360
You are lovelier than
I ever could have imagined.

692
01:36:37.800 --> 01:36:39.800
Elizabeth.

693
01:36:50.080 --> 01:36:54.000
I keep my promises!

694
01:37:20.840 --> 01:37:25.720
- Tell me what happened.
- No. I know what I have to do.

695
01:37:25.880 --> 01:37:30.680
- No. Victor! You can't do this!
- I love her. What would you do?

696
01:37:30.840 --> 01:37:34.440
- Leave her in peace.
- My father would do this.

697
01:37:34.600 --> 01:37:37.800
Your father is dead.

698
01:37:37.960 --> 01:37:42.680
- Then there's nothing left to lose.
- Nothing but your soul.

699
01:39:47.040 --> 01:39:50.920
Live!

700
01:39:52.440 --> 01:39:55.640
No!

701
01:40:22.120 --> 01:40:25.680
Live...

702
01:40:55.920 --> 01:40:59.760
Say my name.

703
01:40:59.920 --> 01:41:04.760
Please, say my name.

704
01:41:06.040 --> 01:41:11.480
Remember!
You must remember.

705
01:41:11.640 --> 01:41:16.000
Elizabeth.

706
01:41:23.200 --> 01:41:26.200
That's it.

707
01:41:26.960 --> 01:41:31.280
That's it, you remember.

708
01:41:33.320 --> 01:41:36.280
That's it.

709
01:41:40.040 --> 01:41:43.640
Now. stand.

710
01:41:54.880 --> 01:41:57.720
Yes, yes...

711
01:42:20.320 --> 01:42:23.800
You remember!

712
01:43:11.240 --> 01:43:13.160
She's beautifuI.

713
01:43:16.600 --> 01:43:20.040
- She's not for you.
- Come!

714
01:43:22.840 --> 01:43:26.040
Elizabeth?

715
01:43:26.200 --> 01:43:29.760
Say my name!

716
01:43:32.200 --> 01:43:35.680
Elizabeth.

717
01:43:41.000 --> 01:43:44.560
Elizabeth!

718
01:43:45.800 --> 01:43:50.080
You're beautifuI.

719
01:43:52.520 --> 01:44:00.400
- Say my name.
- Elizabeth. come to me.

720
01:45:04.960 --> 01:45:08.640
Say my name, Elizabeth.

721
01:45:08.800 --> 01:45:11.320
Vic...

722
01:45:11.480 --> 01:45:14.320
That's right, Elizabeth.

723
01:45:14.480 --> 01:45:19.240
- Victor...
- No, you're mine!

724
01:45:20.800 --> 01:45:25.520
- You're mine.
- Leave her alone!

725
01:45:25.680 --> 01:45:29.280
- Get away. She's mine.
- She said my name!

726
01:45:29.440 --> 01:45:32.680
She's mine!

727
01:46:22.520 --> 01:46:29.440
All that I once loved
lies in a shallow grave, by my hand.

728
01:46:32.880 --> 01:46:36.840
I followed the traiI he left for me.

729
01:46:37.000 --> 01:46:42.000
North. Always north.

730
01:46:42.160 --> 01:46:45.360
For months now...

731
01:46:45.520 --> 01:46:48.400
With one intent:

732
01:46:49.240 --> 01:46:52.720
To kilI him.

733
01:46:54.200 --> 01:46:56.640
Now...

734
01:47:00.520 --> 01:47:03.880
...I'm tired.

735
01:47:06.320 --> 01:47:12.720
I'm so very, very tired.

736
01:47:27.840 --> 01:47:31.040
What did he say?

737
01:47:31.240 --> 01:47:34.800
He's dead.

738
01:47:34.960 --> 01:47:40.280
He died raving
about some phantom.

739
01:47:40.440 --> 01:47:42.640
What is it out there, Captain?

740
01:47:46.640 --> 01:47:51.080
He told me a story that...

741
01:47:52.960 --> 01:47:56.560
...couldn't be true.

742
01:47:56.720 --> 01:48:01.480
He was mad. I think.

743
01:48:04.680 --> 01:48:07.160
A warming breeze!

744
01:48:09.360 --> 01:48:14.440
- The ice will melt yet.
- And what then, Captain?

745
01:48:20.720 --> 01:48:24.160
- We head north.
- No!

746
01:48:46.000 --> 01:48:48.240
Who are you?

747
01:48:51.560 --> 01:48:54.360
He never gave me a name.

748
01:49:21.040 --> 01:49:28.040
- Why do you weep?
- He was my father.

749
01:49:30.240 --> 01:49:36.360
"And I gave my heart to know
wisdom, madness and folly,

750
01:49:36.520 --> 01:49:42.800
- and I perceived that all is
vanity and vexation of spirit."

751
01:49:42.960 --> 01:49:46.920
"For in much wisdom is much grief,

752
01:49:47.080 --> 01:49:51.920
- and he that increaseth knowledge,
increaseth sorrow."

753
01:49:52.080 --> 01:49:58.800
"For God shall bring every work and
every secret thing into judgement,

754
01:49:58.960 --> 01:50:03.440
- whether it be good,
or whether it be eviI."

755
01:50:11.440 --> 01:50:15.240
- Captain...
- He has a right to bear witness.

756
01:50:25.960 --> 01:50:29.200
Jesus, it's breaking up!

757
01:50:38.320 --> 01:50:41.000
Get back to the ship, Captain.

758
01:50:41.160 --> 01:50:43.640
Leave the damn torch!

759
01:50:46.520 --> 01:50:49.560
Come with us.

760
01:50:49.720 --> 01:50:52.960
I am done with man.

761
01:51:05.280 --> 01:51:08.320
Help!

762
01:51:11.920 --> 01:51:14.440
Captain!

763
01:52:22.640 --> 01:52:26.920
Where to now, Captain?

764
01:52:36.760 --> 01:52:40.240
Home.
